{{Navbar-Global Gas Infrastructure Tracker}}
'''Great Basin Gas Transmission Company Pipeline System''' is an operating natural gas pipeline in the United States.<ref name="r30800f">{{Cite web|url=https://www.eia.gov/naturalgas/pipelines/EIA-NaturalGasPipelineProjectsAug2026.xlsx|title=Natural Gas Pipeline Projects, August 2026 release, U.S. Energy Information Administration|website=eia.gov|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref><ref name="r4a3bf2">{{Cite web|url=https://nnbw.com/news/2015/jul/27/blm-oks-natural-gas-pipeline-right-of-way|title=nnbw.com|website=nnbw.com|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>

==Location==
The pipeline runs from Wieland Flat Compressor Station (Ruby Pipeline interconnect), Nevada to Elko City Gate, Nevada.<ref name="r4a3bf2" /><ref name="rd46939">{{Cite web|url=https://regulations.justia.com/regulations/fedreg/2014/07/21/2014-17046.html|title=regulations.justia.com|website=regulations.justia.com|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>

==Project Details==
*'''Owner: '''Paiute Pipeline Co<ref name="rd46939" />
*'''Capacity: '''22 MMcf/d<ref name="r30800f" /><ref name="rd46939" />
*'''Length: '''35 mi<ref name="rd46939" /><ref name="r30800f" /><ref name="r4a3bf2" />
*'''Diameter: '''8 in<ref name="rd46939" /><ref name="rb7ac71">{{Cite web|url=https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2015-02-03/pdf/2015-01995.pdf|title=Federal Register, Vol. 80, No. 22, 3 February 2015, Notices|website=govinfo.gov|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>
*'''Status: '''Operating<ref name="r30800f" /><ref name="r4a3bf2" />
*'''Start year: '''2015<ref name="r30800f" />

==Background==
Paiute Pipeline Company applied to the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission to build the project in Elko County, Nevada. The company said it would provide 21,994 dekatherms a day of service.<ref name="rb7ac71" /> The Bureau of Land Management said the project would expand gas capacity to Elko for growing residential and business load and the energy needs of mining operations.<ref name="r4a3bf2" />

The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission issued its certificate on May 14, 2015.<ref name="r4a3bf2" /> In July 2015, the Bureau of Land Management signed a decision record approving a right-of-way for about 35.2 miles of new 8-inch pipe.<ref name="r4a3bf2" />

